            "review_text": "Traveler of the Wild\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam66 contributions\n0\nChecked back again. Great beers but those heads are too big! Need to fix fix guys:)\nNov 2019\nAs per my previous write-up. Friendly service, excellent selection of beers and reasonable prices, limited but delicious food menu BUT.......................on my last 3 visits they have been definitely short-pouring in terms of the size of the head on the beer. \n\nFor my own drinks the frothy head was approaching 15 percent of the pint and I saw one drink served to another customer where it was quite literally approaching a fifth of the glass. \n\nIn a proper craft beer pub the heads on the beers should be maximum 5% of the total volume of the glass. If over-sized lined glasses are used then the liquid must reach the line on the glass to denote a 16oz (US pint) a 20oz (UK pint) or indeed a metric 500ml glass. \n\nI want to highlight that mispouring of craft beers in HCMC is fairly common and Rehab are not the only guilty party, other places do it too. \n\nHowever, for a guaranteed honest full pour go to Te Te Taphouse (district 1) or Saigon Craft (district 7). They train their staff on how to carefully and properly pull a pint from the taps. Happy drinking!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 6, 2019",
