            "review_title": "Review at Rehab Station - Social Dining",
            "review_text": "Baolan\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam60 contributions\n1\nWaited one hour although we had pre-ordered\nJul 2019 • Friends\nBooked a table for my team (less than 20 people) for a casual dinner and pre-booked all the mains. \n\nWaiters were very keen on selling their expensive beers and we asked at least 4 times to check on the kitchen why the food took so long although we had preordered and booked in advance. \n\nThe answer: “it’s coming, it’s coming”\n\nAfter an hour I got sick of waiting and went down to the “manager” Son - who just said “sorry I the guys upstairs didn’t give the order to the kitchen, they just did so a few minutes ago. It’s coming” \n\nAvoid unless you enjoy bad customer service (and smelling people smoking weed next to your table)\nRead more\nWritten July 26, 2019\nRio Tuan T\nDear Baolan,\n\nMy apologize for making you and your team waited more than one hour for your food, even though it was ordered in advance. I take full responsibility for my staff mistake and deeply regret the inconvenience that it must have caused you. \nThat night a new bar staff forgot to hit the send button of your order to the kitchen from our POS system. That’s no excuse, and I again apologize for my untrained staff. In the future, I will be sure to ask the kitchen staff prepare the preordered food straight away, instead of having a bar staff order it through our POS System to avoid any delay.\nThank you for bringing this issue to my attention so I can train my staff more carefully to avoid any inconvenience to our future customer. I’m confident your next experience with our restaurant will be up to the highest standard that you’ve come to expect from,\n\nSincerely,\nRead more\nWritten August 6, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
